# Why a second instance of alphabeta.inc changed the default Worker::search, and the fix

Method: src/search.cpp compiled alone with the PC flags (g++ 15.2 ucrt64, -std=c++20 -O3 -DNDEBUG
-DFORGE_NNUE_HIDDEN=256 -ffp-contract=off -fno-fast-math -march=znver5) plus -fdump-tree-optimized
-fdump-ipa-inline; the default Worker::search (_ZN5forge6Worker6searchERNS_5BoardEPNS_11SearchStackEiiib)
extracted with fn_extract.py (--norm: SSA/decl numbers normalised). base = opus-O3 0d99f02 (one instance).

## v1: second instance (search_corr_margins), both instances call tune.inc's lmp_threshold
$ diff base_body.txt v1_body.txt   (normalised GIMPLE body, 3222 statements each)
1889c1889
<   if (CheckExtensionDepth.N_N <= depth_N)
---
>   if (depth_N >= CheckExtensionDepth.N_N)
$ grep CheckExtensionDepth (un-normalised): one of the 8 copies of the check-extension test gets SSA
  version 397 instead of 247, so GCC's canonical operand order (lower SSA version first) flips it:
base_raw.txt:3006:  if (depth_293 >= CheckExtensionDepth.289_397)
base_raw.txt:3027:  if (CheckExtensionDepth.289_247 <= depth_293)
base_raw.txt:3049:  if (CheckExtensionDepth.289_233 <= depth_293)
v1_raw.txt:3027:  if (depth_293 >= CheckExtensionDepth.289_397)
v1_raw.txt:3049:  if (CheckExtensionDepth.289_259 <= depth_293)

IPA inliner decisions for the default Worker::search ('Considering ... to be inlined into' lines):
lmp_threshold (one caller in AL1 s198) is inlined early in base; with a second caller it is left to
the IPA inliner in v1, which shifts the SSA numbering of the default search:
$ diff base_inl.txt v1_inl.txt
1,13c1,14
