Machine code of v1 vs the AL1 s198 lock (codegen_compare.sh, default alpha-beta only):
function                                          insns_A  insns_B differing  mod64_A  mod64_B
forge::Worker::search(forge::Board&                  2413     2409       150       32       32
(the same 2413 -> 2409 instructions / 150 lines that branch opus-C6 reports for its second instance)

## v2: lmp_threshold marked [[gnu::always_inline]] (rejected)
$ diff base_body.txt v2_body.txt
214,215c214,216
<   _N = (short unsigned int) _N;
<   if (_N == _N)
---
>   capped_N = (const int) _N;
>   _N = (int) _N;
>   if (_N == capped_N)
1473d1473
<   _N = depth_N * depth_N;
1475c1475,1476
<   _N = _N + pretmp_N;
---
>   _N = depth_N * depth_N;
>   _N = pretmp_N + _N;
(always_inline changes the early inliner's order: TTEntry::score_usable is no longer narrowed to
 16 bits and lmp_threshold's depth*depth moves)

## v3 = final: the second instance calls its own copy, lmp_threshold_corr_margins (src/search/corr_margins.inc)
$ diff base_body.txt v3_body.txt   -> 0 lines
$ diff of the un-normalised GIMPLE (SSA versions kept, only decl-uid suffixes normalised) -> 0 lines
Machine code: see codegen_compare.log (default alpha-beta 2413 = 2413 instructions, 0 differing, mod 64 32 = 32).
